Thanks! I've simplified the model as you specified, and since the particular problem I'm working on allows this, I've fixed the loading from C to Y to be 1. The convergence is definitely much better -- the R-hat is 1.011 after only 2,000 burn-in iterations, although it takes some more iterations for effective sample size to reach the recommended levels. Still, this is a massive improvement. And I see what you mean about the model being hard to estimate -- I'll think about ways to mitigate this, because in practice, I plan to have the MCMC samples from the blavaan estimation be part of an active learning loop, so I'll be running the same estimation on slightly different datasets iteratively.

